    Bug 2008667 - In immutable recurrence rules, remember calculated occurrences for later reuse. r=mkmelin

    If a recurrence rule is immutable, the occurrences will never change, so there is no need to
    calculate them more than once. In this patch I've added code to run through the calculation only
    once (and only as far as is needed at the time), remember the output, then use the remembered
    values for subsequent calls.

    This optimisation makes the earlier `recurrenceEndDate` optimisation unnecessary, so I've removed
    it. There is still potential for further optimisation using precalculated event start and end
    times, but I've not investigated it yet.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D278089

